# Publishing to Amazon ECR

This repo's release workflow (`.github/workflows/release.yml`) publishes
the container image and the Helm chart to Amazon ECR as OCI artifacts.
The workflow is fully wired — it just needs one-time AWS-side prep, then
arming via a repo variable.

Until it is armed, merges to `main` still bump the version and push the
release tag; only the publish jobs stay skipped.

## One-time AWS setup

Create the two ECR repositories (image and chart):

```bash
aws ecr create-repository \
  --repository-name ${project_name} \
  --region us-east-1

aws ecr create-repository \
  --repository-name ${project_name}-chart \
  --region us-east-1
```

Configure an IAM role that GitHub Actions can assume via OIDC. The
trust policy should match this repository's OIDC subject (e.g.
`repo:${project_owner}/${project_name}:*`). Permissions needed:
`ecr:GetAuthorizationToken`, `ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability`,
`ecr:CompleteLayerUpload`, `ecr:InitiateLayerUpload`, `ecr:PutImage`,
`ecr:UploadLayerPart`, `ecr:DescribeRepositories`, and
`ecr:DescribeImages` against both repository ARNs.

## Repository configuration

Add these Actions secrets (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions):

| Secret               | Value                                                    |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ECR_AWS_ACCOUNT_ID` | 12-digit AWS account id                                  |
| `ECR_REGION`         | ECR region, e.g. `us-east-1`                             |
| `ECR_ROLE_ARN`       | ARN of the OIDC role, e.g. `arn:aws:iam::<id>:role/<r>`  |

Then arm the publish jobs by setting the repo **variable**
`ECR_PUBLISH_ENABLED=true`. `workflow_dispatch` runs bypass this gate so
the pipeline can be tested standalone before arming.

## What the workflow publishes

- **Image** — `<registry>/${project_name}:<semver>` (multi-arch via
  docker buildx bake), signed with cosign, with SLSA provenance
  attached.
- **Chart** — `oci://<registry>/${project_name}-chart` at the
  tag-derived version (chart version = tag without the leading `v`,
  `appVersion` = tag) — lockstep with the image and binary;
  `Chart.yaml` keeps a `0.0.0-dev` placeholder by design. The push is
  idempotent: an already-published chart version is skipped.

The GitHub Release itself (goreleaser binary archives) is
registry-independent and publishes regardless of the ECR gate below.

where `<registry>` is
`<account-id>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com`.

Cosign signatures and SLSA attestations are stored in ECR alongside the
artifacts they cover — verify with `cosign verify` against the pushed
digest.

## Local push (no CI)

`just helm-push` packages the chart and pushes it to the registry named
by the `ECR_REGISTRY` environment variable. Auth is handled separately:

```bash
export ECR_REGISTRY=<account-id>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com
aws ecr get-login-password --region <region> | \
  helm registry login "$ECR_REGISTRY" --username AWS --password-stdin
just helm-push
```
